                <pb facs="0416" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.857/662: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-05T18:00:00-04:00">May 5, 1942—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>631. Contrary to the last sentence in the Department’s 605, April 30, 8 p.m., you
                    should not take joint action with the British Embassy in this matter but you
                    should request the assurances for the Government of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
